High-Priority Topics & Must-Know Problem Types:

1. Arrays and Strings
Sorting & Searching – Binary search, quicksort, mergesort
Two Pointers Technique – Removing duplicates, merging sorted arrays
Sliding Window – Longest substring without repeating characters, maximum sum subarray
Prefix Sum – Range sum queries, subarray sum problems
Monotonic Stack – Next greater/smaller elements

2. Linked Lists
Reversal – Reverse a linked list, k-group reversal
Cycle Detection – Floyd’s cycle detection algorithm
Partitioning & Merging – Merge two sorted linked lists, reorder list

3. Trees & Binary Search Trees (BSTs)
Tree Traversals – Preorder, inorder, postorder (recursive & iterative)
Lowest Common Ancestor (LCA) – Finding LCA in a BST or binary tree
Depth vs. Breadth Analysis – BFS vs. DFS traversal strategies
Binary Search Trees (BSTs) – Validate BST, insert/delete nodes

4. Graphs
Graph Traversal – Depth-first search (DFS), breadth-first search (BFS)
Topological Sorting – Course scheduling problem
Shortest Path Algorithms – Dijkstra’s algorithm, Bellman-Ford
Connected Components – Union-Find, cycle detection

5. Backtracking
Classic Recursion Problems – Generating permutations, combinations
Sudoku Solver – Constraint-based search
N-Queens Problem – Placing queens without conflicts

6. Heaps & Priority Queues
Top-K Elements Problems – Kth largest/smallest element
Merging Sorted Lists – Merge k sorted linked lists
Median in a Stream – Using a min-max heap approach

7. Tries (Prefix Trees)
Word Search & Autocomplete – Implementing a trie
Prefix Matching – Longest common prefix
Dictionary-Based Problems – Spell checker, word break problem

8. Dynamic Programming (DP)
Knapsack & Subset Problems – 0/1 Knapsack, partition equal subset sum
Longest Common Subsequences – LCS, LIS, edit distance
Matrix-Based DP – Unique paths, minimum path sum

9. Bit Manipulation
Finding Odd Occurrences – XOR technique
Power of Two & Bit Counting – Checking if a number is a power of two
Bitmasking Techniques – Subset generation, dynamic programming optimizations

10. Math & Number Theory
Prime Numbers & GCD – Sieve of Eratosthenes
Modulo Arithmetic – Handling large numbers efficiently
Combinations & Permutations – Factorial-based counting
